        "original_id": "5d0ca12d-d3d5-5db7-94cb-15f37053dbb5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ridley Scott, Elmer Clifton, D. W. Griffith, Joseph Henabery\n- Roles: film director, producer, actor, collaborator, mentor\n- Films: Alien, Blade Runner, Gladiator, The Martian, The Birth of a Nation, Intolerance\n- Topics: film careers, notable works, career transition\n\nFacts:\n- Ridley Scott was born on 30 November 1937 and is an English film director and producer.\n- Elmer Clifton appeared in The Birth of a Nation in 1915 as a collaborator of D. W. Griffith.\n- Elmer Clifton appeared in Intolerance in 1916 before ending his acting career in 1917.\n- In 1917, Elmer Clifton gave up acting to concentrate on work behind the camera, with D. W. Griffith and Joseph Henabery as his mentors.\n- Ridley Scott had his commercial breakthrough with the science-fiction horror film Alien in 1979.\n- Ridley Scott's best known works include Blade Runner in 1982, Gladiator in 2000, and The Martian in 2015.\n- Gladiator won the Academy Award for Best Picture.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
